song of ascents. In my distress I cried to the LORD, and He answered me.","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Deliver my soul, O LORD, from lying lips and a deceitful tongue.","verse":2}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Meshech","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":1,"href":"?bref=Ps.120.5","rawReference":"Ps.120.5"}],"ruleId":"Meshech::Meshech::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Meshech"},"text":"Woe to me that I dwell in Meshech, that I live among the tents of Kedar!","verse":5}],"id":"Meshech","label":"Meshech","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Meshech::Meshech::source_verse_citation","scope":"source_verse_citation","senseReview":"Original complete headword and source opening identify a named person, people, or place. Promotion requires a capitalized whole name and the original article explicitly citing this same BSB verse. No arbitrary qualifier stripping or book-title inference. This citation-constrained rule was reviewed once globally; unmatched contexts remain excluded.","sourceHeadwordId":"Meshech","term":"Meshech"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Meshech","sourceTitle":"Meshech"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.120.1-134.3","r":"Ps.120.1-134.3","rawR":"Ps.120.1-134.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.120.1-134.3","value":"Ps.120.1-134.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 120–134"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," These short, appealing songs were sung during pilgrims’ journeys to Jerusalem for the national festivals three times per year (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.16.16","r":"Deut.16.16","rawR":"Deut.16.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.16.16","value":"Deut.16.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Deut 16:16"},"). The title of these psalms includes the Hebrew word for stairs, which some take to mean “ascending to Jerusalem.” These psalms (sometimes called the Songs of Ascents) take the reader on a pilgrimage to Jerusalem to praise God for his goodness to Israel throughout history."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.120.1-134.3","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":134,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":120,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.120.1-134.3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[120,121,122,123,124,125,126,127,128,129,130,131,132,133,134],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"804bdc0d4264fc96adf7bf16357af3c33f1b33647dde7b70863e764ccb4e0941","sourceItemName":"Ps.120.1-134.3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7297,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.120.1-134.3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.120.1-134.3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.120.1-7","r":"Ps.120.1-7","rawR":"Ps.120.1-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.120.1-7","value":"Ps.120.1-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 120"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This short, individual lament expresses the psalmist’s trust that the Lord will deal with deceptive evildoers. It also laments living as a stranger among hateful liars. The psalmist’s picture of his life in a foreign land might have been a reality as he set out for Jerusalem, or it might depict his feelings and concerns as he begins his pilgrimage. Overwhelmed with injustice, he trusts God and looks forward to arriving in the Lord’s presence."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.120.1-7","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":120,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":120,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.120.1-7","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[120],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6aa94f0234e1a6866bfb4d6b3c838fa532f9c279d21362c3af42be27a76e2214","sourceItemName":"Ps.120.1-7","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7298,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.120.1-7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.120.1-7","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.120.1-2","r":"Ps.120.1-2","rawR":"Ps.120.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.120.1-2","value":"Ps.120.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"120:1-2"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist is surrounded by ",{"c":["liars"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," so he makes his lament ",{"c":["to the"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt-divine-name","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," the only one who can help him."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.120.1-2","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":120,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":120,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.120.1-2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[120],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d0b2d094dfbe63c05be4a2ec45af34dcbf927bf49eb25153f0816b42081207d2","sourceItemName":"Ps.120.1-2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7299,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.120.1-2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.120.1-2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.120.3-4","r":"Ps.120.3-4","rawR":"Ps.120.3-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.120.3-4","value":"Ps.120.3-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"120:3-4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist dialogues with the liars who surround him. He feels reassured that the Lord will judge them. • The Divine Warrior (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.7.12-13","r":"Ps.7.12-13","rawR":"Ps.7.12-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.7.12-13","value":"Ps.7.12-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:12-13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.11.4-6","r":"Ps.11.4-6","rawR":"Ps.11.4-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.11.4-6","value":"Ps.11.4-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:4-6"},") will throw ",{"c":["sharp arrows"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["glowing coals"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," on the liars."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.120.3-4","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":120,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":120,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.120.3-4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChap